      "detail": "The negotiated cipher has a 64-bit block, so ciphertext blocks begin colliding after roughly 34.4 GB under a single key. With a 48-hour rekey interval this SA processes about 1091.79 GB per key, which is 31.775x the bound. At the observed 50.55 Mbps this SA reaches the bound 91 minutes after each rekey.",
      "recommendation": "Move to a 128-bit block cipher (AES-GCM-256). If that cannot be scheduled immediately, cut the rekey interval so that less than 34.4 GB passes under any single key \u2014 that is mitigation, not a fix.",
